/-!
# Local rings of a normal integral curve

Source: Stacks Project, Curves, Tag 0CCK, proof of Lemma `lemma-flat`, first sentence;
Varieties, Tag 0B8Y; Algebra, Tag 00PD.
(blueprint: lem-a1-normal-curve-local-principal-domains)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Local rings of a normal integral curve are Noetherian of dimension zero or one,
are fields in dimension zero and DVRs in dimension one, and are principal ideal domains.
Source: Stacks Project, Curves, Tag 0CCK, proof of Lemma `lemma-flat`, first sentence;
Varieties, Tag 0B8Y; Algebra, Tag 00PD.
(blueprint: lem-a1-normal-curve-local-principal-domains)

Proof:
1. Every ideal of the field `k` is zero or the unit ideal, so `k` is Noetherian.
   Thus `Spec k` is locally Noetherian (`pqf-def-locnoeth`). The curve structure is
   locally of finite type (`def-pc-curve`), so `pqf-lem-locnoeth-lft` makes `Y`
   locally Noetherian.
2. Choose a Noetherian affine open around `y` (`pqf-def-locnoeth`). Its germ map
   realizes the stalk as localization at the point's prime ideal by clause (c) of
   `lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-stalk-localization`. Apply
   `lem-weil-pbc-localization-noetherian` to conclude the stalk is Noetherian.
3. Normality gives an integrally closed domain (`def-sbc-normal-dominant-galois`),
   and a scheme stalk is local (`def-pc-scheme`). The stalk dimension is at most
   the dimension one of the curve (`def-pc-curve`, `def-pc-dimension`). Its zero
   ideal is prime, so its dimension is nonnegative. By the chain-length definition
   (`def-weil-pbc-krull-dimension-ring`), the dimension is zero or one.
4. In dimension zero, the maximal ideal is zero: otherwise it and the zero prime
   form a strict chain of length one (`def-weil-pbc-krull-dimension-ring`). The
   residue field (`def-weil-residue-field`) then identifies the stalk with a field.
5. In dimension one, apply `lem-sc-normal-dim1-dvr` to this Noetherian normal local
   domain to obtain a discrete valuation ring. No perfection or separability is needed.
6. Every ideal of a field is generated by zero or one; every ideal of a DVR is principal
   (`def-sc-discrete-valuation-ring`). Together with integrality this gives a PID.
-/
theorem IsIntegralCurve.stalk_local_principal_domains
    {k : Type u} [Field k] {Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    [IsIntegralCurve f] (hY : IsNormalScheme Y) (y : Y) :
    IsNoetherianRing (Y.presheaf.stalk y) ∧
      ringKrullDim (Y.presheaf.stalk y) ≤ 1 ∧
      (ringKrullDim (Y.presheaf.stalk y) = 0 → IsField (Y.presheaf.stalk y)) ∧
      (ringKrullDim (Y.presheaf.stalk y) = 1 →
        IsDiscreteValuationRing (Y.presheaf.stalk y)) ∧
      (ringKrullDim (Y.presheaf.stalk y) = 0 ∨ ringKrullDim (Y.presheaf.stalk y) = 1) ∧
      IsDomain (Y.presheaf.stalk y) ∧ IsPrincipalIdealRing (Y.presheaf.stalk y) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
